  "worked_solution": "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\pi x),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\pi x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\pi x=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=n,$ where $n$ is an integer.",
